tations of western romances -- 10. Genealogy of the romances -- 11. Common elements of the romances: oral background vs textual interference -- 12. Reception -- Conclusions."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Roderick Beaton."},"Includes index.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Bibliography: p. 211-255."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-gr---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Romances, Byzantine","History and criticism"]}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"PA5165 .B43 1989"},{"@edition":"19","@authority":"ddc","#text":"883/.02/09"}],"relatedItem":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Cambridge studies in medieval literature ","partNumber":[6]}},{"@type":"series","titleInfo":{"title":"Cambridge studies in medieval literature","partNumber":"6"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990019162210203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0521333350"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^88034658^"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"18873272"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000121086569","#text":"Dumbarton Oaks Research Library and Collection, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"PA5165 .B43 1989"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"PA5165 .B43 1989"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":["Dumbarton Oaks","Widener"]},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990019162210203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"001916221"}},"processingDate":"2026-08-14T04:22Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DLC"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"881122"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20131021"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990019162210203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.8 using\n\t\t\t\t\tMARC21slim_MODS3-8_XSL2-0.xsl (Revision 2.79 2025/03/28)"}},{"titleInfo":{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"medieval Greek romance"},"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Beaton, Roderick","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Criticism, interpretation, etc."}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"London"}},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"Routledge","dateIssued":"1996","edition":"2nd ed., rev. and expanded.","issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xx, 301 p. : maps ; 24 cm."},"tableOfContents":"Pt. I. 1071-1204. 1. The Twelfth-Century Background. The Byzantine empire in the twelfth century. Levels of language and levels of literature. Literacy, books and readers. East meets West? 2. The Literary Tradition. Mimesis and rhetoric. Realism and the individual. 3. The 'Proto-Romance', Digenes Akrites. Precursors of the romance. 'Digenes': story and versions. The original 'Digenes'. 4. The Renaissance of a Genre. 5. The Twelfth-Century Texts -- Pt. II. 1204-1453. 6. The First 'Modern Greek' Literature. The rise of vernacular literature. Significance and development of the 'political' verseform. 7. The Original Romances: The Texts and their Stories. The texts: authorship, date, manuscript tradition. The stories. 8. The Original Romances: Narrative Structure. 9. Translations and Adaptations of Western Romances. 10. Genealogy. The twelfth-century and Hellenistic romances. East meets West. 11. Orality. The theories. Critique of the theories. A new proposal. 12. Reception -- Afterword: The Medieval Greek Romance Since 1987.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Roderick Beaton."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 270-293) and index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-gr---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Romances, Byzantine","History and criticism"]}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"PA5165 .B43 1996"},{"@edition":"20","@authority":"ddc","#text":"883/.0209"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0415120322 (hbk.)"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0415120330 (pbk.)"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^95023528^"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"32821715"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990069026570203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000121086569","#text":"Dumbarton Oaks Research Library and Collection, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"PA5165 .B43 1996"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"PA5165 .B43 1996"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"PA5165 .B43 1996"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":["Dumbarton Oaks","Lamont","Widener"]},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990069026570203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"006902657"}},"processingDate":"2024-03-16T05:11Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DLC"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"950622"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20050319"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990069026570203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)"}},{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"An  "},"title":"introduction to modern Greek literature "},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Beaton, Roderick","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Criticism, interpretation, etc."}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Oxford "}},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York "}}],"issuance":"monographic","agent":[{"namePart":"Clarendon Press "},{"namePart":"Oxford University Press"}],"dateIssued":"1999","edition":"2nd ed., rev. and expanded"},"language":[{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},{"languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"}},{"languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"gre"}}],"physicalDescription":[{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xiv, 420 p., maps ; 22 cm."},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"map"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"A readable introduction to Greek poetry and fiction published since national independence in 1821, this is the first full-length study to be devoted to the literature of this period, seen as a whole, and including developments up to the present day. Highlighting those writers and works which have enjoyed critical or popular acclaim, it emphasizes the relationships which link one work with another and with its historical context. No knowledge of Greek is assumed and all quotations are given both in Greek and in English. An Introduction to Modern Greek Literature will be an important source for both specialists and general readers, bringing to light a rich but neglected part of modern European literature\"-- Publisher's website."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Roderick Beaton."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (p. [376]-407) and index."},{"@type":"language","#text":"English text with Greek quotations."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-gr---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Greek literature, Modern","History and criticism"],"temporal":"20th century"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Greek literature, Modern","History and criticism"],"temporal":"19th century"},{"@authority":"fast","temporal":"1800-1999"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"PA5225 .B43 1999"},{"@edition":"21","@authority":"ddc","#text":"889.09"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0198159749"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"41211964"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990078437380203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"PA5225 .B43 1999x"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Widener"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990078437380203941","priorrecordid